          "statement": "Aristolochene synthase catalyzes the conversion of $(2E,6E)$-farnesyl pyrophosphate (FPP) into the bicyclic sesquiterpene aristolochene, the precursor to fungal toxins (PR-toxin).\n(a) The reaction initiates with ionization of FPP and cyclization to the 10-membered macrocyclic intermediate **germacrene A**. Provide the curved-arrow mechanism for this 1,10-cyclization.\n(b) Protonation of germacrene A triggers a second cyclization to form the bicyclic eudesmyl carbocation, followed by a concerted 1,2-methyl shift. Trace these rearrangements and state the role of active-site aromatic residues in preventing premature water quenching.",
