          "statement": "(a) Write out the complete stepwise mechanism for the synthesis of racemic phenylalanine starting from phenylacetaldehyde ($\\text{PhCH}_2\\text{CHO}$), ammonium chloride ($\\text{NH}_4\\text{Cl}$), and sodium cyanide ($\\text{NaCN}$).\n(b) To prepare enantiomerically pure $(S)$-phenylalanine directly, modern pharmaceutical chemistry employs chiral auxiliaries or chiral organocatalysts. Outline the catalytic asymmetric Strecker reaction using a chiral cyclic guanidine or BINOL-derived catalyst, explaining how facial selectivity is achieved during cyanide addition.",
