          "title": "Saponification Value and Molecular Weight Calculation of Triacylglycerols",
          "statement": "A $2.000\\text{ g}$ sample of a pure synthetic triacylglycerol (TAG) was completely saponified with $50.00\\text{ mL}$ of $0.5000\\text{ M}$ ethanolic $\\text{KOH}$. The unreacted alkali required $28.40\\text{ mL}$ of $0.5000\\text{ M HCl}$ for complete neutralization in a phenolphthalein back-titration. A blank titration without fat required $49.80\\text{ mL}$ of $0.5000\\text{ M HCl}$.\n(a) Calculate the Saponification Value ($SV$) of the triacylglycerol in $\\text{mg KOH/g}$.\n(b) Determine the average molecular weight ($M_{\\text{TAG}}$) of the triacylglycerol.\n(c) If the fat is a simple triglyceride (all three fatty acyl chains are identical saturated acids), identify the fatty acid.",
